powerpc/powernv: restore NPU2 / NVLink 2.0 support for the AC922's V100s

Local, not for upstream. Mainline removed the in-kernel NPU2 driver (npu-dma.c, v5.3/v5.13), which is what
gave an IBM AC922 its coherent NVLink path between the POWER9 nest MMU and Tesla V100-SXM2 GPUs. This puts
back "stage 1" only: the OPAL wrappers, pnv_pci_get_npu_dev()/pnv_pci_get_gpu_dev(), the NPU_NVLINK PHB
type and its PE setup, and the boot-time translation context (pnv_npu2_map_lpar_dev() ->
opal_npu_map_lpar() + opal_npu_init_context()) that every NVLink GPU needs before the GPU driver issues
DMA. NVIDIA's proprietary nvidia-uvm then runs ATS in "driver mode" on top of it.

